AWS DevOps Interview Preparation Series — Day 1 🚀

Topic: Amazon EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)

As part of my AWS DevOps Interview Preparation Series, today we’ll cover one of the most critical AWS services — Amazon EC2.
Whether you’re preparing for a DevOps or SRE interview, these 30 real-world EC2 questions will help you test and strengthen your fundamentals. 👇

🔹 EC2 — Top 30 Interview Questions for DevOps Engineers

What is Amazon EC2 and why is it used in DevOps environments?
What are the different EC2 instance types and their ideal use cases?
Explain On-Demand, Reserved, and Spot Instances.
How does EC2 Auto Scaling help maintain availability and cost efficiency?
What are EC2 Security Groups and how are they different from Network ACLs?
What’s the difference between EBS and Instance Store volumes?
How do you take a snapshot of an EBS volume and create an AMI?
What is an AMI and how do you share it across regions or accounts?
What are EC2 placement groups and what types are available?
What is the lifecycle of an EC2 instance?
What happens when you stop vs terminate an EC2 instance?
How do you connect to an EC2 instance securely using SSH?
What is the use of EC2 user data and metadata?
How do you attach and detach EBS volumes to running instances?
What is an Elastic IP address and when should you use it?
What are key pairs in EC2 and how are they managed?
How can you monitor EC2 performance metrics using CloudWatch?
What are the benefits of using EC2 launch templates over launch configurations?
How do you automate EC2 provisioning with Terraform or CloudFormation?
How do you troubleshoot EC2 instances that are unreachable via SSH?
What is the difference between public and private EC2 instances in a VPC?
How do you resize (scale up or down) an EC2 instance?
How do you configure load balancing for EC2 instances?
What is hibernation in EC2 and when should you use it?
How do you ensure high availability for EC2-hosted applications?
What are EC2 instance retirement notices and how do you handle them?
How can you optimize EC2 cost in production environments?
How does AWS Systems Manager help in managing EC2 instances?
What’s the difference between EC2 Spot Fleet and EC2 Auto Scaling Group?
How can you ensure data persistence and backup for EC2 instances?

💡 Pro Tip:
 Mastering EC2 is key for any DevOps Engineer. Focus on automation (Terraform, Ansible), scaling, monitoring, and cost optimization — these are frequently discussed in real interviews.
